      "title": "Finding the Rank or Nullity of a Matrix Given a Description of the Column or Null Space"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "c5a678d7-b079-5756-9dd3-2365a68c9acb",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Let $A$ be a $3\\times 5$ matrix. If $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$, find $\\text{dim(Null}(A)).$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=5,$ and since $B$ is formed by $3$ vectors, $\\text{rank}(A)=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 3+\\text{nullity}(A) & =5 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =5-3 \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
